# XCU time
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# The page leaves the results of a plain "time" simple command with
# redirections or in a pipeline unspecified, so the tests call the
# utility as "command time" and by a direct exec, which the page names as
# specified ways.

assertion  XCU.time.001
anchor     utilities/time.html#STDERR
anchor     utilities/time.html#OPTIONS
class      required
since      1992
says       time -p writes the lines real, user and sys, each followed by a
           decimal number with at least one digit after the radix
           character, to standard error (a leading empty line and extra
           text after are allowed).
test       t/001-p-format.sh

assertion  XCU.time.002
anchor     utilities/time.html#EXIT STATUS
class      required
since      1992
says       time exits with the status of the utility.
test       t/002-status.sh

assertion  XCU.time.003
anchor     utilities/time.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/time.html#STDOUT
class      required
since      1992
says       time runs the utility with the arguments given and writes the
           timing on standard error, not on standard output.
test       t/003-runs.sh

assertion  XCU.time.004
anchor     utilities/time.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/time.html#STDERR
class      required
since      1992
says       The real time reported covers the run of the utility: for sleep 2
           it is at least one second.
test       t/004-real-time.sh

assertion  XCU.time.005
anchor     utilities/time.html#EXIT STATUS
class      required
since      1992
says       time exits 127 when the utility cannot be found and 126 when it
           is found but cannot be run.
test       t/005-not-found.sh
